// as the cloud-top height field, and everything about the form is read off it:
// its gradient is a surface normal, how far it stands above the coverage
// threshold is optical depth, and how it rises along the sun azimuth is whether
// a lobe is standing between this point and the sun.
//
// Three separate things darken a cloud and only one of them is N.L. A face that
// turns away from the sun is dark; a face in the lee of the lobe in front of it
// is dark whichever way it points; and the underside of any lobe is dark because
// the light had to cross the whole body to reach it. The first alone gives a
// noise field with no undersides, which is what this deck used to be.
