  // fwidth is the ocean footprint of this pixel in metres, already carrying the
  // grazing-angle stretch that makes the footprint along the view an order of
  // magnitude larger than the one across it. Everything finer than that has
  // been folded into the mean normal above by the mip chain and the vertex
  // grid, and can only be represented as a distribution. Both the reflection
  // and the sun lobe below read this one number, so they stay consistent and
